{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggDHLmitDLE3zQnXozF2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, so no grosz gets lost.\n\n**The bug:** `split_cents` in `money.py` used `total // people` and dropped the remainder.\n\n**The fix:** it now uses `divmod` and gives the leftover grosze to the first people, one each. The shares always add up to the total and never differ by more than one grosz.\n\n**Tests:** I added two tests to `test_money.py`. One checks the 1 zł / 3 case. The other checks that the shares sum to the total and differ by at most 1, for every total from 0 to 249 grosze split between 1 and 7 people. Both failed before the fix, and all 5 tests pass now.\n\nOne thing to be aware of: the first person in the list always pays the extra grosz. If you'd rather that rotate between people, or go to someone specific like whoever paid the bill, that's an easy change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":524,"cache_read_input_tokens":18955,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":524},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a17d026-ddac-4128-89d0-70e5026655bb","uuid":"8c22b499-04c6-412b-b725-9ca09231befc","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:14:11.826Z","request_id":"req_011CggDHLXLhZZv2ZZ7mY6NT"}
